          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em intermediate value theorem
            (IVT) is a fundamental principle of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analysis"} analysis
            which allows one to find a desired value by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interpolation"} interpolation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon [0,1] \to \mathbb{R}
            from an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            (all with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(0)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(1)
          %p
            The IVT in its general form was not used by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclid"} Euclid
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+geometry"} Euclidean geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Archimedes"} Archimedes
            made general arguments in which a quantity is approached from above and below, allowing him not only to trisect the angle but also to calculate
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pi"} π
          %p
            As normally stated, the IVT is not valid in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %em approximate
            zero, or to strengthen the hypothesis to require the functions satisfy additional properties or have other structures, such as locally nonconstancy and lifting to locators in functions in the given example below. Even interpreted classically, these are prima facie weaker results.
          %h2#statements_and_proofs Statements and Proofs
          %h3#classical_ivt Classical IVT
          #classical.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              (classical IVT, assuming
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon [a,b] \to \mathbb{R}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              from a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+interval"} closed interval
              to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a) \lt 0
              while
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(b) \gt 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              in the unit interval such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(c) = 0
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:\mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}
              be defined as
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo −
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(x) \coloneqq (b - a) x + a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:[0,1] \to \mathbb{R}
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \coloneqq f \circ g
            %p
              By
              %a{:href => "connected+topological+space"} this example
              the interval
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected topological space
              (this is where
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
              is used).
            %p
              By
              %a{:href => "connected+topological+space"} this prop.
              also its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f([0,1]) \subset \mathbb{R}
              is connected. By
              %a{:href => "connected+topological+space"} this example
              that image is itself an interval. This implies the claim is true for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %h3#constructive_ivt_with_weakened_conclusion Constructive IVT with weakened conclusion
          #conclusion.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p (constructive IVT with weakened conclusion)
            %p
              For real numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon [a,b] \to \mathbb{R}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointwise+continuous+function"} pointwise continuous function
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+interval"} closed interval
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [a, b]
              to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a) \lt 0
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(b) \gt 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              there exists a point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_\epsilon
              in the interval such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mi ϵ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|f(c_\epsilon)|} \lt \epsilon
          .proof
            %h6#proof_of_theorem_
              Proof of Theorem
              = succeed "\u2060" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#conclusion"}
            %p
              This proof originally appeared in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Frank20"} Frank 2020
            %p
              Let us inductively define the following
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequences"} sequences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_0 \coloneqq a
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_0 \coloneqq b
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mi n
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_n \coloneqq \frac{a_n + b_n}{2}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi max
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi min
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                        %mo +
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi ϵ
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_n \coloneqq \max\left(0, \min\left(\frac{1}{2} + \frac{f(c_n)}{\epsilon}, 1\right)\right)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo −
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{n + 1} = c_n - \frac{d_n (b - a)}{2^{n + 1}}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo −
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{n + 1} = b_n - \frac{d_n (b - a)}{2^{n + 1}}
            %p Then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo −
                        %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_n - a_n = \frac{b - a}{2^n}
            %p
              and the sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_n
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+sequence"} Cauchy sequence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \lt n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi m
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo −
                        %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert c_m - c_n \vert \leq \frac{b - a}{2^m}
            %p
              Lemma: For every natural number
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \leq m
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert f(c_j) \lt \epsilon
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a_m) \lt 0
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(b_m) \gt 0
            %p
              When
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a_0) = f(a) \lt 0
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(b_0) = f(b) \gt 0
            %p
              Now, assume that the above lemma is true for a particular
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \leq m
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert f(c_j) \lt \epsilon
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi m
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \leq m + 1
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert f(c_j) \lt \epsilon
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 f(c_m) \lt -\epsilon
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 f(c_m) \gt \epsilon
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert f(c_m) \vert \gt \epsilon
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi c
                            %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi ϵ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 f(c_m) \lt -\epsilon
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi m
                        %mo ≔
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_m \coloneqq 1
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mrow
                            %mi m
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ≔
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mi m
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{m + 1} \coloneqq a_m
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mrow
                            %mi m
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ≔
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mi m
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_{m + 1} \coloneqq c_m
                %p
                  so that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mrow
                            %mi m
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{m + 1} \lt 0
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi b
                            %mrow
                              %mi m
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mo &gt;
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_{m + 1} \gt 0
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi c
                            %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo &gt;
                          %mi ϵ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 f(c_m) \gt \epsilon
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi m
                        %mo ≔
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_m \coloneqq 1
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mrow
                            %mi m
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ≔
                        %msub
                          %mi c
                          %mi m
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{m + 1} \coloneqq c_m
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mrow
                            %mi m
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ≔
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mi m
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_{m + 1} \coloneqq b_m
                %p
                  so that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
